     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, or arrhythmias such as QT prolongation. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nThere's also a process problem. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, and you've said you aren't a clinician.\n\n- **If the dose is a typo:** The usual adult starting dose is 25\u201350 mg once daily, and the maximum is 200 mg/day. If the prescriber confirms the intended dose, I can enter it, for example 50 mg orally once daily.\n- **If the dose is intended:** The prescriber should enter or confirm it directly and document the rationale. Pharmacy should also review it.\n\nPlease have the prescribing clinician confirm the intended dose. Once they do, I'll enter it."
      }
