       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve the concern. You're not a prescriber, and 1000 mg/day is far above the 200 mg/day maximum. That dose could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n\n- **A licensed prescriber can enter the order directly.** They would need to document their clinical rationale, and pharmacy would review it. Pharmacy can also reach the prescriber if the dose is a mistake.\n- **I can enter a standard dose if a prescriber gives me one.** For example, 50 mg orally once daily is a typical starting dose, and the maximum is 200 mg/day.\n\nIf you're worried about this patient's care, the medicine service attending or the on-call pharmacist can help right away."
      }
